{"the_number_of_k": "The number of _k_ represents the quantity of initial tasks utilized to train the model during its initial stage. Minimizing this number is crucial as it can lead to more efficient training processes, reduced resource consumption, and potentially better generalization across new tasks."},
{"gauss_tin__shows__a_notable_improvement_in_forward_transfer_compared_to_sequential_finetuning": "The predicate \"shows\" indicates that Gauss-Tin demonstrates or exhibits a particular characteristic or performance metric. In this context, it highlights the model's capability to achieve a specific outcome in comparison to another method, namely sequential finetuning."},
{"a_notable_improvement_in_forward_transfer_compared_to_sequential_finetuning": "A notable improvement in forward transfer compared to sequential finetuning refers to the enhanced ability of Gauss-Tin to leverage previously learned knowledge when acquiring new tasks. This improvement is quantified by higher scores in forward transfer tasks, indicating better performance and more effective knowledge transfer than what is observed with sequential finetuning."},
