{"superior_performance": "Superior performance in this context refers to the higher effectiveness and better results achieved by joint training compared to other training methods like sequential fine-tuning. It is characterized by higher scores in both forward and backward transfer metrics, indicating better retention and application of learned knowledge across tasks."},
{"joint_training__scores__up_to_6_97_for_forward_transfer": "The predicate \"scores\" in this context refers to the performance metrics achieved by the joint training method in comparison to other methods like Gauss-Tin and sequential fine-tuning. It indicates how well the joint training method performs in terms of forward transfer, which is the ability to apply knowledge from previous tasks to new tasks."},
{"up_to_6_97_for_forward_transfer": "The object \"up to 6.97 for forward transfer\" describes the highest performance score achieved by the joint training method in the context of forward transfer. This score represents the effectiveness of joint training in leveraging knowledge from previous tasks to improve performance on new tasks, serving as a benchmark against which other methods are compared."},
{"joint_training__scores__19_57_for_backward_transfer": "The predicate \"scores\" in this context refers to the performance metric achieved by the joint training method in the backward transfer scenario. Backward transfer measures a model's ability to retain knowledge from previously learned tasks after being trained on new tasks, indicating how well the model can avoid catastrophic forgetting."},
