{"combination_of_prompts_and_gmm": "The combination of prompts and GMM refers to the integrated use of task-directed prompts and Gaussian Mixture Models (GMM) within the Gauss-Tin method for the Continual Learning (CL) framework. This integration aims to enhance the adaptability and robustness of the learning model by leveraging the complementary strengths of both components."},
{"combination_of_prompts_and_gmm__leads_to__notable_performance_gains_in_forward_transfer": "The predicate \"leads to\" indicates a causal relationship where the integration of prompts and GMM results in significant improvements. Specifically, this integration causes or brings about notable performance gains, suggesting that the combined approach is more effective than using either component alone."},
{"notable_performance_gains_in_forward_transfer": "Notable performance gains in forward transfer refer to significant improvements in the performance metrics when applying the integrated approach of prompts and GMM in scenarios where knowledge is transferred forward to new tasks. This is evidenced by superior average performance scores compared to using only prompts or only GMM."},
