{"methods_employing_only_gmm": "The methods employing only GMM refer to techniques that utilize Gaussian Mixture Models (GMM) without the integration of prompts within the Gauss-Tin method for the Continual Learning (CL) framework. These methods rely solely on the statistical modeling capabilities of GMM to handle data characteristics and learning tasks."},
{"methods_employing_only_gmm__achieved__average_scores_of_3_0325": "The predicate \"achieved\" indicates that the methods employing only GMM have reached a certain level of performance as measured by average scores. This suggests that these methods have been evaluated and their effectiveness quantified in the context of the CL framework."},
