{"the_maximum_input_length": "The maximum input length refers to the predefined limit on the number of tokens that the BART model can process in a single input. In this context, it is set to 1024 tokens to ensure that the model can handle the diverse and complex tasks it is designed for."},
{"learning_rate": "The learning rate is a critical hyperparameter in machine learning models that determines the step size at each iteration while moving toward a minimum of a loss function. It directly influences the speed and stability of the training process."},
{"learning_rate__was_fixed_at__5_10_5": "The phrase \"was fixed at\" indicates that the learning rate was set to a specific, unchanging value throughout the training process. This decision is crucial as it affects how the model converges to an optimal solution."},
{"5_10_5": "The value 5 \u00d7 10 [\u2212] [5] represents a very small number, specifically 0.00005. This extremely low learning rate ensures that the model makes very small updates to its weights during training, which can help in achieving a more stable and precise convergence."},
