{"our_goal__is_to_minimize__the_number_of_k_as_much_as_possible": "The phrase \"is to minimize\" indicates a strategic objective within the research or methodology, specifically aiming to reduce or lower a certain parameter or variable to achieve optimal performance or efficiency."},
{"the_number_of_k_as_much_as_possible": "The number of _k_ as much as possible refers to the desire to reduce the quantity of initial tasks (denoted as _k_) used in the training phase of a machine learning model. This reduction is pursued to enhance the model's efficiency and adaptability in learning new tasks without compromising performance on previously learned tasks."},
{"gauss_tin__shows_a_notable_improvement_in__forward_transfer_compared_to_sequential_finetuning": "The phrase \"shows a notable improvement in\" indicates that Gauss-Tin demonstrates a significant enhancement or superior performance in a specific aspect compared to another method, in this case, sequential fine-tuning."},
{"forward_transfer_compared_to_sequential_finetuning": "Forward transfer compared to sequential finetuning refers to the ability of a model to apply knowledge gained from previous tasks to improve performance on new tasks. Gauss-Tin excels in this area by not only avoiding performance degradation but also by enhancing learning in new contexts, as evidenced by its positive scores across various tasks."},
