{"sequential_fine_tuning_for_dk_5": "Sequential fine-tuning for _Dk_ 5 refers to a method where a model is trained on an initial set of tasks and then fine-tuned sequentially on new tasks. In this context, _Dk_ 5 represents the fifth task in a sequence of tasks used to evaluate the model's performance in both forward and backward transfer metrics."},
{"sequential_fine_tuning_for_dk_5__scores__3_74": "The predicate \"scores\" indicates the performance metric achieved by the sequential fine-tuning method on task _Dk_ 5. This score is used to evaluate how well the model has adapted to the new task while retaining knowledge from previous tasks."},
{"gauss_tin__mitigates__catastrophic_forgetting": "The predicate \"mitigates\" in this context refers to the ability of Gauss-Tin to reduce or lessen the negative impact of catastrophic forgetting. By maintaining positive scores across tasks and avoiding the sharp decline observed in other methods, Gauss-Tin effectively addresses the challenge of retaining knowledge from previous tasks when learning new ones."},
